      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Nutrition – Concept and Role in Life"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Carbohydrates, proteins, and fats constitute macronutrients that provide energy and structural components.",
        "Fat-soluble vitamins (A, D, E, K) are stored in the liver and fatty tissues, whereas water-soluble vitamins (B-complex, C) need regular daily supply.",
        "Vitamin A deficiency causes Night Blindness, while Vitamin C deficiency results in Scurvy.",
        "Vitamin D deficiency leads to Rickets in children and Osteomalacia in adults.",
        "Essential mineral deficiencies include Iron leading to Anaemia and Iodine leading to Goitre."
      ],
      "id": "70ae2dc"
    },
